# IMG-04 — Meaningful alt text on raw images; empty alt for decorative

## Rationale

Screen-reader accessibility; raw `<img>` elements need an `alt` attribute, and
decorative images need `alt=""`.

Shopify's `image_tag` filter is different: when the input is a Shopify image
object, it uses the object's `alt` text by default. Do not ask for an explicit
`alt:` argument in that case unless the theme intentionally needs to override
the object's admin-managed alt text.

## How to check

```bash
bun "<skill-dir>/scripts/cli.ts" check images <file>
```

Flags raw `<img>` tags with no `alt` attribute at all. It does not flag
`image_tag` usage.

## How to fix

**Auto-fix** raw `<img>` when alt can come from a Shopify image source:

- `image.alt`, `media.alt`, or alt on section/block image settings
- pass an alt variable into snippets that render raw `<img>`

**Do not fix** by adding `alt:` to `{{ image_object | image_tag }}` just to
mirror `image_object.alt`; that is redundant because `image_tag` already uses
the Shopify image object's alt text.

**Propose** when the image is not tied to an image/media object (hardcoded assets,
external URLs, decorative icons). The developer must supply alt text or confirm
decorative `alt=""` — the agent should not invent content alt.

**Manual check (low severity):** Even when alt is wired from objects, add a
manual checklist item for the merchant to verify alt text is set correctly on
those images in Shopify admin.
